            question: Can you identify departments with more than 100 staff members?
query: using the emp.Employees and mst.Department tables to retrieve department names (mst.DepartmentName) and the count of active employees (COUNT(emp.Id)) for emp.University_Id = 1 and emp.ActionStatusId = 1, grouped by department, filtered to only include those with more than 100 employees, and ordered by employee count in descending order.

question: Which departments have more than 100 employees?
query: SELECT mst.DepartmentName,COUNT(emp.Id) AS EmployeeCount FROM emp.Employees emp
INNER JOIN mst.Department mst ON mst.Id = emp.DepartmentId
WHERE emp.University_Id = 1  AND emp.ActionStatusId = 1  
GROUP BY mst.DepartmentName
HAVING COUNT(emp.Id) > 100
ORDER BY EmployeeCount DESC;

question: What are the department names where the employee count exceeds 150?
query: SELECT mst.DepartmentName,COUNT(emp.Id) AS EmployeeCount FROM emp.Employees emp
INNER JOIN mst.Department mst ON mst.Id = emp.DepartmentId
WHERE emp.University_Id = 1  AND emp.ActionStatusId = 1  
GROUP BY mst.DepartmentName
HAVING COUNT(emp.Id) > 150
ORDER BY EmployeeCount DESC;




question: Provide the department- and designation-wise active staff count
query: select DepartmentName,DesignationName  ,count(Id)Staff from emp.vw_EmployeesList where UniversityId =1 and ActionStatusId =1 and EmpId =0
group by DepartmentName,DesignationName   order by DepartmentName

question: What is the headcount of IT staff on leave this month?
query: SELECT ld.EmployeeId, ev.EmployeeName, ev.DepartmentName, ev.DesignationName, COUNT(*) AS LeavesTaken FROM emp.LeaveDateWiseDetails ld INNER JOIN emp.vw_EmployeesList ev ON ld.EmployeeId = ev.Id WHERE LOWER(ev.DepartmentName) LIKE '%information technology%' AND ld.LeaveDate >= CONVERT(varchar(10), DATEFROMPARTS(YEAR(GETDATE()), MONTH(GETDATE()), 1), 120) AND ld.LeaveDate <= GETDATE() AND ld.ActionStatusId = 4 AND ld.ApprovedActionStatusId = 4 GROUP BY ld.EmployeeId, ev.EmployeeName, ev.DepartmentName, ev.DesignationName;

question: give me the department name where number of employees are more than 100
query: SELECT mst.DepartmentName,COUNT(emp.Id) AS EmployeeCount FROM emp.Employees emp
INNER JOIN mst.Department mst ON mst.Id = emp.DepartmentId
WHERE emp.University_Id = 1  AND emp.ActionStatusId = 1  
GROUP BY mst.DepartmentName
HAVING COUNT(emp.Id) > 100
ORDER BY EmployeeCount DESC;


